  "tags": ["data-access", "api-composition", "replication"],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Cross-service data access is one of the hardest problems in microservices. You cannot join across service databases. You must use APIs, replication, or composition."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Key Concepts"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "key-terms",
      "data": {
        "terms": [
          {
            "term": "API Composition",
            "definition": "Aggregating data from multiple service APIs."
          },
          {
            "term": "Data Replication",
            "definition": "Copying data from one service to another."
          },
          {
            "term": "CQRS View",
            "definition": "A read model built from events of other services."
          },
          {
            "term": "Shared Database Anti-Pattern",
            "definition": "Directly accessing another service database (avoid)."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Strategies"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "data": {
        "headers": ["Strategy", "Description", "Consistency"],
        "rows": [
          ["API Composition", "Call multiple services and combine", "Real-time"],
          ["Data Replication", "Copy data to local store", "Eventual"],
          ["CQRS View", "Build read model from events", "Eventual"],
          ["Shared DB (avoid)", "Direct database access", "Coupled"]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "API Composition"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "API composition calls multiple services and combines results. It is real-time but adds latency and chattiness. Use it for simple aggregations."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Data Replication"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Data replication copies data from the owning service to other services. This enables local reads without network calls. Data is eventually consistent."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "CQRS View"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "A CQRS view builds a read model by subscribing to events from other services. The read model is optimized for queries and is eventually consistent."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Architecture"
      }
    },
